  "slug": "phases-symtft-1132",
  "summary": "Recent preprints extend symmetry-protected classification to half-chiral symmetry, spectral localizer invariants, and fractal lattice geometries.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these preprints is symmetry-constrained classification of lattice topological phases, with the protecting symmetry or invariant generalized in each case. One study identifies phases protected by half-chiral symmetry, where chiral symmetry acts on only one sublattice, and characterizes them with real-space invariants and zero-energy modes. A second generalizes the spectral localizer to unify Z and Z2 invariants for hinge modes, Dirac nodes, and valley boundary modes. A third realizes SSH, Haldane, Qi-Wu-Zhang, and Z2 insulators on fractal lattices, including site-eliminated, projected, and patterned constructions. What is new is the widening of protecting symmetries and invariants rather than a single shared method. The fractal study transfers established models to fractal geometries, while the other two works redefine the symmetry or invariant that controls classification.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
